From 0b1fda72f5e69856b45cce3463f46a5aa0c5b1e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:52:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] perf(kanban-sync): key a links pass's state.db reads
 by value instead of re-reconciling every 300 s

An unchanged board was reconciled again every LINKS_MAX_AGE_S only to re-read
session sources, compression lineage and profile homes from state.db. A pass now
records the answers each board's reconcile used and the next pass replays those
reads; the board is reconciled again only when an answer changed. Inside a pass
the 300 s source cache is bypassed, so a recorded answer is never older than its
pass. A pass that swallowed a failed read records no key and keeps the max-age
retry.

Also counts links_refresh background checks by decision (cold/skip/age/inputs)
and accounts the rebuild separately: the existing links_refresh scope counts
checks, cache hits included.

Task: t_eeeeee0000000018
